---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const GITHUB_URL = 'https://github.com/reynsu/nativelens';
const NPM_URL = 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/@reynsu/nativelens-cli';
const VERSION = '0.2.1';
---

<Base>
  <main>
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">v{VERSION} · MIT · React Native · Detox</p>
      <h1>nativelens</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        E2E testing for React Native that captures the <strong>React component tree</strong>
        — props, state, hooks — at every action, not just the native view hierarchy or
        screenshots. Every failed assertion ships with the exact fiber state that produced
        it, and a <strong>diagnosis agent</strong> tells you whether you're looking at a
        test bug or a real bug.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#install">
          Get started
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHAT IT IS -->
    <section class="what">
      <p class="eyebrow">What it is</p>
      <h2>Detox drives the test. nativelens reads the fiber.</h2>
      <p>
        Detox boots your app in an emulator and drives interactions. nativelens runs
        inside the app as a <strong>probe</strong>, subscribed to React fiber commits
        via <a href="https://github.com/aidenybai/bippy" rel="noopener">bippy</a>. Every
        action ends with a snapshot of the component tree — every prop, every hook value,
        every <code>testID</code>, indexed and shipped to the dashboard over a WebSocket.
        When a test fails, the diagnosis agent reads that snapshot alongside your source
        and returns a structured verdict.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- INSTALL -->
    <section id="install" class="install">
      <p class="eyebrow">Quick install</p>
      <h2>Three commands to running tests.</h2>
      <pre class="code-block"><code><span class="comment"># In your Expo project root</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span>npx @reynsu/nativelens-cli init
<span class="prompt">$</span>pnpm install
<span class="prompt">$</span>nativelens run                  <span class="comment"># harness + dashboard on :7777</span></code></pre>
      <p class="fine-print">
        Expo + EAS dev client only in v0.1. Bare React Native is on the roadmap. Full
        walkthrough in the <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/packages/cli/README.md`} rel="noopener">CLI
        README</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- FEATURES -->
    <section class="features">
      <p class="eyebrow">What you get</p>
      <h2>Built around the snapshot.</h2>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Probe-based snapshots</h3>
          <p>
            React fiber commits trigger a serialized component tree — every prop, hook
            value, and <code>testID</code> indexed to its owning fiber. Captures what
            screenshots can't see: stale state, missing handlers, hook desync.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Diagnosis agent</h3>
          <p>
            <code>nativelens diagnose</code> reads the failure snapshot, your spec, and
            the screen source, then emits a structured verdict: <code>real-bug</code>,
            <code>test-bug</code>, <code>flaky</code>, or <code>env-issue</code> — with
            evidence, confidence, and an optional patch.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Local-first</h3>
          <p>
            Subscription path via <code>claude login</code> uses your Pro/Max plan, not
            pay-per-token API. The <code>ollama</code> backend is a fully offline escape
            hatch — no credentials, no cloud, no telemetry.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3>Time-travel dashboard</h3>
          <p>
            Replay any past run frame-by-frame with the component tree alongside the
            screenshot. Past runs are persisted under <code>.nativelens/runs/</code> —
            the dashboard is just a thin reader on top of the same NDJSON the live path
            writes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CALIBRATION SECTION (one of nativelens's distinctive features) -->
    <section class="calibration">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why the diagnosis agent is trustworthy</p>
      <h2>The eval gate measures itself.</h2>
      <p>
        Every release of the diagnosis agent runs against 15 synthetic React Native
        failure cases. Calibration v4 ships at <strong>14/15 floor accuracy</strong>
        and <strong>100% high-confidence calibration</strong> — when the agent says
        "high", it's right. The thresholds are measured baselines, not aspirational
        targets, and the gate runs nightly to catch regression from prompt or
        SDK drift.
      </p>
      <p class="fine-print">
        Calibration history + per-case results live in the
        <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/packages/cli/src/eval/thresholds.ts`} rel="noopener">
          thresholds.ts inline log
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- FOOTER -->
    <footer>
      <div class="footer-inner">
        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="noopener">github</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href={NPM_URL} rel="noopener">npm</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">MIT</a>
        </div>
        <p class="footer-meta">
          Built with <a href="https://astro.build" rel="noopener">Astro</a>.
          Source: <a href="https://github.com/reynsu/nativelens-site" rel="noopener">nativelens-site</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Hero */
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* Generic helpers */
  .fine-print {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  /* Features grid */
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
  }

  .feature-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .feature-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .feature-card p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Calibration section */
  .calibration p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  /* Footer */
  footer {
    padding: 3rem 0 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .footer-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .footer-links span {
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
  }

  .footer-meta {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
